//! Dou Dizhu (斗地主): game records (JSONL) → candidate-action gm-shards. Rules and
//! frames: `gmrules::games::doudizhu` (the simulator's code); every record is
//! REPLAYED by those rules — the deal (a partition of the 54 cards), every bid, every
//! play (legal, by the right seat, in turn) and the recorded returns — before its
//! frames are written ([`crate::traj`]).
//!
//! There is no public human data: the corpus is DouZero self-play generated by
//! `scripts/generate_doudizhu.py` (the public DouZero ADP / WP agents play every
//! card; a hand-strength heuristic bids — `meta.bidding`), end to end with
//! `scripts/fetch_doudizhu.sh`. `gmdata doudizhu random` writes the same format from
//! uniformly random play (tests, smoke runs).
//!
//! Record format (one game per line, `.jsonl` / `.jsonl.gz`; card ids as OpenSpiel's:
//! `c < 52` → rank `c % 13` (3 4 5 6 7 8 9 T J Q K A 2), suit `c / 13`; 52 / 53 = the
//! black / coloured joker):
//!
//! ```text
//! {"id": "dz0-17",                               (optional; default file:line)
//!  "hands": [[17 card ids], [17], [17]],          seats 0..2 as dealt (before the kitty)
//!  "kitty": [3 card ids],
//!  "face_up": card id,                            the card dealt face up: its holder bids first
//!  "auction": [[seat, bid], ...],                 0 = pass, 1..3 (OpenSpiel's auction)
//!  "plays": [[seat, play], ...],                  "Pass" or the play's OpenSpiel string:
//!                                                 every card by rank ("34567", "3444",
//!                                                 "(BWJ)(CJ)"), airplanes / four-with-two
//!                                                 with kickers as "main-kickers"
//!                                                 ("333444-56", "7777-4455")
//!  "returns": [r0, r1, r2],                       (optional) checked against the replay
//!  "agents": ["douzero_wp", ...],                 (optional) who played each seat's cards
//!  "q": [[i, [[play, Q], ...]], ...],             (optional) teacher values of plays[i]'s
//!                                                 decision (the generator's top moves)
//!  "meta": {...}}                                 (optional) copied into the sample meta
//! ```
//!
//! The deal becomes the rules' chance events canonically — face-up position = the
//! first bidder's first card, each hand dealt in ascending card order (the face-up
//! card first) — so frames depend only on what the rules show (rank counts, the
//! face-up rank). A play with kickers becomes its decisions (main, then one kicker per
//! unit: `gmrules::games::doudizhu::play_events`).
//!
//! Filters: `--agent NAME` (repeatable) keeps only the per-seat streams of seats
//! whose cards NAME played; `--hq` = `--agent douzero_adp --agent douzero_wp` (the
//! strong DouZero agents; drops e.g. the supervised `douzero_sl` or `random` seats).
//! Games nobody bid on (no play phase) are kept: their streams are auction frames
//! of the same bidding policy as every other record's.
//!
//! Teacher soft targets (`--soft-k K --soft-temp AGENT=T`, experimental): the
//! records' DouZero Q values of each play decision become `softmax(Q / T)` over the
//! listed full plays (T per agent: ADP's Q is in points, WP's in win-probability
//! units), marginalised onto the factored decisions — the main decision gets the
//! mass of every full play through it, each kicker decision the conditional mass of
//! the plays sharing the recorded prefix — written as `tgt.action_probs_idx/val`
//! (candidate indices).
//!
//! ```sh
//! uv run python scripts/generate_doudizhu.py --out data/doudizhu/raw --games 1000000 --workers 32
//! gmdata doudizhu convert --input data/doudizhu/raw --out data/doudizhu/train --hq
//! gmdata doudizhu random  --out data/doudizhu/random/r.jsonl.gz --games 1000
//! ```

